.TH "FWD LS" "1" "2026-08-12" "fwdit" "fwd ls Manual"
.SH NAME
fwd\-ls \- List managed sessions with live backend status.
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B fwd ls
[OPTIONS]
.SH DESCRIPTION
List managed sessions with live backend status.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
\fB\-\-all\-projects\fP
Show sessions from every locally tracked project instead of only the
current project.
.TP
\fB\-c,\fP \-\-columns <str>
Show selected columns by comma-separated name; repeat to combine.
Session names remain as row identity.
.TP
\fB\-\-names\fP
Show only session names.
.TP
\fB\-\-backends,\fP \-\-backend
Show session names and backends.
.TP
\fB\-\-statuses,\fP \-\-status
Show session names and live statuses.
.TP
\fB\-\-stop\-after\fP
Show session names and queued stop-after state.
.TP
\fB\-\-running\fP
Show session names and current run durations.
.TP
\fB\-\-tmux\fP
Show session names and remote tmux names.
.TP
\fB\-\-local\-dirs,\fP \-\-local\-dir
Show session names and local project directories.
.TP
\fB\-\-last\-attached\fP
Show session names and last-attachment times.
.TP
\fB\-\-ids\fP
Show session names and provider identifiers.
.TP
\fB\-\-ports\fP
Show session names and local port forwarding.
.TP
\fB\-\-format\fP <auto|rich|markdown|json>
Output format: auto uses Rich in a terminal and Markdown otherwise.
[default: auto]
.TP
\fB\-\-json\fP
Render structured output as JSON; shorthand for --format json.
.SH EXIT STATUS
\fB0\fP indicates success. Any nonzero value indicates an error.
.SH REPORTING BUGS
Report issues at \fIhttps://github.com/Sid-MB/fwd/issues\fP.
.SH SEE ALSO
\fBfwd\fP(1)
